Package: coherentSurv
Type: Package
Title: Coherent Survival Modelling and Dynamic Forecasting
Version: 0.11.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sunday A.", "Adetunji", email = "sundayadetunjisa@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Oluwatimileyin A.", "Adetunji", email = "eniola16.to@gmail.com", role = "aut"))
Description: Provides coherent survival modelling and dynamic forecasting for
    history-dependent recurrent and terminal events. Fits continuous-time
    shared-frailty joint intensity models and generates forecasts conditional
    on observed history at specified landmark times. Computes joint-law
    recurrence burdens, terminal-event risks and restricted survival, with
    calibration assessed through validation diagnostics.
    Provides automatic coarsened-history integration, sparse propagation,
    finite-path and continuous-time targeted estimation, scalable finite-support
    recording-sensitivity bounds, evolving-covariate forecasts, alternative frailty
    distributions, weighted conformal calculations, and calibration diagnostics.
    Adds baseline binary-treatment g-formula estimates, cross-fitted
    intensity targeting and influence-function contrasts under explicit
    consistency, exchangeability, positivity and censoring assumptions.
    Observation assumptions and numerical diagnostics are retained in returned
    objects; prognostic forecasts and causal treatment contrasts are distinct.
    Uses a compiled C++17 core with an R interface and examples for calling
    the same implementation from 'Python' through 'rpy2' or 'Rscript'.
